<DocsLayout title="Installation" description="Install RelayCore on your system">
  <h1>Installation</h1>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Rust 1.70+ (if building from source)</li>
    <li>OpenSSL (Linux) or SecureTransport (macOS)</li>
    <li>CA certificate installation requires admin privileges</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cargo (Recommended)</h2>
  <pre><code>cargo install relay-core-cli</code></pre>
  <p>The file this puts on PATH is <code>relay-core-cli</code>. Command examples in these docs use <code>relay-core</code>, the command installed by <code>npm install -g @relay-core/cli</code>.</p>

  <h2>npm</h2>
  <pre><code>npm install -g @relay-core/cli</code></pre>

  <h2>Pre-built Binaries</h2>
  <p>Download from <a href="https://github.com/relaycraft/relay-core/releases">GitHub Releases</a>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>macOS (Apple Silicon)</li>
    <li>macOS (Intel)</li>
    <li>Linux (x86_64)</li>
    <li>Linux (ARM64)</li>
    <li>Windows (x86_64)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Linux Installation</h3>
  <pre><code>tar -xzf relay-core-cli-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
sudo mv relay-core-cli /usr/local/bin/relay-core
relay-core --version</code></pre>

  <p>Linux binaries are built as <strong>glibc-linked (gnu)</strong> and ship the Deno / V8 script engine. The <code>musl</code>-static variant is no longer published — <code>rusty_v8</code> has no musl prebuilds, and shipping musl binaries without V8 would break JS scripts on Linux. If you need a musl build, compile from source with <code>cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl</code>.</p>

  <h3>macOS Installation</h3>
  <pre><code>tar -xzf relay-core-cli-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
sudo mv relay-core-cli /usr/local/bin/relay-core
relay-core --version</code></pre>

  <h3>Windows Installation</h3>
  <p>Extract the ZIP and add <code>relay-core-cli.exe</code> to PATH as <code>relay-core.exe</code>.</p>

  <h2>Build from Source</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/relaycraft/relay-core
cd relay-core
cargo build --release
./target/release/relay-core-cli --version</code></pre>

  <h2>Verify Installation</h2>
  <pre><code>relay-core --version
# relay-core 0.14.0</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
